# Working directories — probes, sweeps, logs and pre-images from the build
# sessions.  1,587 MB untracked before the 2026-07-30 deploy, almost none of it
# publishable: `_to_delete/` alone held 288 MB (a half-finished copy of site/),
# `_tika/` 264 MB of probe output.  These are how findings were measured and are
# worth keeping ON DISK; they are not worth carrying in the repository.
_abhia/
_ana/
_appcache*/
_charcensus/
_codepage/
_diaA/
_entry*/
_fnprobe/
_hyphen/
_kankha/
_khua/
_maa0*/
_navprobe/
_pre7/
_pre8/
_regress/
_revbak_*/
_sama/
_screen/
_seam/
_tika/
_to_delete/
_vcache*/
_vism/
node_modules/

# Byte-code and pre-images.  A pre-image is how this project recovers from a bad
# build (nav.json was restored from one twice), so they are kept ON DISK — but
# there are ~70 HANDOFF.md.bak_*, 137 nav.json.bak*, and a .pre* beside most
# builders, and none of them belongs in the history.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.bak[0-9]*
*.pre[0-9a-z_]*
*damaged_by*

# Session scratch under _xc/ — staging copies and pre-images from the
# 2026-08-01 prune. The verification scripts and linksk_fixed/ maps in the
# same directory ARE tracked; only these are not.
_xc/linksk_prePrune/
_xc/reader2_*.html
_xc/i18n_v*.js
_xc/sitemin*.tgz
_xc/linksk_classc/
_xc/linksk_preC/
_xc/linksk_rebuild/

# Source PDFs of the Tipiṭaka-Pāḷi-Myanmā-Abhidhāna (23 vols, ~45 MB each) and any
# page images extracted from them.  Same reasoning as the pali/ atthakatha/ tika/
# rules above: public-domain source scans, kept ON DISK, never in the repository.
# Globbed rather than spelled out because macOS stores the name in NFD and a
# literal NFC pattern would silently fail to match.
Tipi*Abhidh*na/

# The sharded frequency table from roadmap step 1: 1,119 shards, 25 MB, and every
# byte of it is regenerated exactly by `_vocab/report.py` from site/. Same
# reasoning as the corpus/ rule above -- it is an intermediate until step 2 ships
# it under site/, at which point it becomes the artefact and this rule goes.
# The scripts and figures beside it ARE tracked; only freq/ is not.
_vocab/freq/

# Step 3's extracted glosses: 187,275 rows, 115 MB across 89 volumes, regenerated
# exactly by `_gloss/glosses.py` from site/ plus site/reader/bold/. Same reasoning
# as _vocab/freq/ -- an intermediate until it ships under site/. The extractor and
# the two verification samples beside it ARE tracked; only by_volume/ is not.
_gloss/by_volume/

# The panel prototype's generated lookup data: ~800 JSON shards, 116 MB, rebuilt
# exactly by `_panel/build_panel_data.py` from ~/GoldenDict, pm12e.csv and DPPN.json.
# Same reasoning as _vocab/freq/ and _gloss/by_volume/ -- generated intermediate.
# It additionally carries dictionary text whose redistribution licences are
# unconfirmed (DPD CC BY-NC-SA, DOP in copyright, the Abhidhana digitisation
# unlicensed), so it must not enter a public repo. The panel code beside it IS
# tracked; only data/ is not.
_panel/data/

# The shipped word-lookup data, built by `_panel/build_lookup.py`: ~5,900 JSON
# shards, 138 MB. Generated exactly from _gloss/by_volume/, _vocab/freq/, the
# PCED dataset's public-domain PED, and DPD's synonym index used as a
# build-time filter only.
#
# MOVED 2026-08-07 from site/lookup/ to stores/lookup/ -- DEPLOY_SCALE §6a, the
# reader's D+B decision. It is no longer "under site/ because that is where the
# reader fetches it from", which is what this comment used to say: the reader
# now fetches it from https://dict.buddha-dhamma.net/, and it stays in the
# repository so that it stays inside the Zenodo deposit. Pages publishes site/
# and nothing else, so moving it out is what drops the deploy from 26,576 files
# to 1,977.
#
# !!! THIS RULE IS ALREADY STALE AND IS KEPT ONLY BECAUSE REMOVING IT IS A
# SEPARATE DECISION. The comment it carried said "it goes into the repo the day
# it is published -- at which point this rule goes". It WAS published, and the
# rule did not go: all 7,319 files are tracked, force-added past this line.
# Ignore rules do not affect already-tracked files, so the rule has no effect
# today and is a trap for whoever next runs a clean rebuild. Reported, not
# resolved, per working principle 5. The licence note in stores/lookup/index.json
# is still the thing to re-read first.
stores/lookup/

# The EVALUATION lookup data and its sources, built by `_panel/build_eval.py`.
# DPD (CC BY-NC-SA, and excluded as a voice by §9 whatever its licence), the
# Abhidhana and PEU (permission unconfirmed -- Ven. Subhuti / the pm12e
# maintainers, and the Ministry question of §8), PPN, and the PCED English and
# Burmese dictionaries. NONE OF IT MAY ENTER A PUBLIC REPO OR A PUBLIC BUILD.
# The panel keeps it behind its own flag (?wle=1), off by default, and
# stores/lookup/ -- Edition + counts + the public-domain PED -- is what ships.
# Regenerated exactly by build_eval.py from ~/GoldenDict plus _dictsrc/.
#
# MOVED 2026-08-07 from site/lookup_eval/ to stores/lookup_eval/, with the rest
# of the stores. Every path below moved with it; the STRUCTURE is unchanged and
# the note about the star still governs it.
#
# !!! `stores/lookup_eval/` (no star) excludes the DIRECTORY, and git cannot
# re-include anything under an excluded directory -- so a `!.../dpd/**` line
# below it silently does nothing.  The star excludes the CONTENTS instead,
# which is what makes the negations below work at all.
stores/lookup_eval/*
!stores/lookup_eval/index.json
!stores/lookup_eval/form/
!stores/lookup_eval/lem/
# DPD is published GZIPPED and only gzipped.  The size argument this line was
# written on has been retired -- the 1 GB Pages cap was never the binding
# constraint (DEPLOY_SCALE §1a: CI checks out 833 MB, and bytes were never the
# problem; the file count and the ten-minute clock were).  The rule STANDS on
# its own terms regardless: 379.2 MB of .json against 43.7 MB of .json.gz, for
# data the panel never requests uncompressed, since index.json lists `dpd` in
# its `gz` array.  The .json stay on disk so a rebuild need not start from
# nothing.
#
# 2026-08-07: r2_upload.sh uploaded all 11,229 of them to the bucket because it
# walked the filesystem instead of `git ls-files`.  They were deleted and the
# script now takes its file list from git.  This rule is why they were never
# meant to leave this machine.
!stores/lookup_eval/dpd/
stores/lookup_eval/dpd/*.json
# !!! THE STAR RULE ATE A WHOLE NEW SUBTREE IN SILENCE (2026-08-09,
# user-reported as "The family data could not be loaded" in production).
# `stores/lookup_eval/family/` was created by rebuild_dpd_families.py; the
# `stores/lookup_eval/*` rule above ignored it; `git add -A` skipped all of
# it; the commit shipped without it; and r2_upload.sh — whose file list is
# `git ls-files` BY DESIGN — correctly uploaded nothing.  Four correct
# mechanisms composing into one invisible absence.  Same convention as dpd/:
# only the .gz is tracked and served; the plain .json stays on this machine.
!stores/lookup_eval/family/
!stores/lookup_eval/family/**/
stores/lookup_eval/family/**/*.json
_dictsrc/

# Build-run stdout/stderr from _panel/ scripts (eval rebuilds, precision sweeps).
# Transient: every run overwrites them, and the numbers that matter are recorded
# in claude/ docs, not here.
_panel/*.out
_panel/*.err
_xc/linksk_named/

# Transfer scratch: tarballs and unpacked copies used to move files between the
# sandbox and this machine. Six of these were swept into commit 649b0059 before
# this line existed.
_xfer/

# The 2026-08-05 line-break-hyphen measurement. Same reasoning as the _xc/ and
# _vocab/freq/ rules above: 118 census shards plus two full row dumps, 2.8 MB,
# regenerated exactly by `_xc/hy1/census.py` and `check_page_fidelity --dump`
# from the PDFs and site/. The FINDINGS and the three probe scripts beside them
# ARE tracked -- they are how the numbers can be re-run; only the output is not.
# Written as `*` on the contents, not on the directory, because git cannot
# re-include anything under an excluded directory (see the lookup_eval note).
_xc/hy1/cen/
_xc/hy1/cache/
_xc/hy1/*.rows.json
_xc/hy1/review.json
_xc/hy1/review.html
_xc/hy1/review_dropped.json
_xc/hy1/edgepg.json
_xc/hy1/pagemap.json
_xc/hy1/offsets.json
# Page renders from pdftoppm, 5 MB. Regenerated from the PDFs in seconds and the
# PDFs themselves are already out of the repo by the pali/ atthakatha/ tika/ rules.
_xc/hy1/pg/
# Block map and its measurements: 118 volume files regenerated by blockmap.py
# from the PDFs in about a minute. The scripts beside them ARE tracked.
_xc/hy1/blocks/
_xc/hy1/blocks2/
_xc/hy1/blocks3/
_xc/hy1/blockgap.json
_xc/hy1/leadcensus.json
_xc/hy1/leadcensus2.json
_xc/hy1/verdicts.json
_xc/hy1/joinscan.json
_xc/hy1/bjoin/
_xc/hy1/bjoin2/
_xc/hy1/edge2.json
